  "question": {
    "text": "A piece of solid weighs&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>gm</mi></math> in open air,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>gm</mi></math> in water and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>gm</mi></math> in a liquid. The relative density of solid and that of liquid are respectively.",
